1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,735
L'Armes Abbey: built on cursed land, where you may end up blessed, or cursed.

2
00:00:03,955 --> 00:00:05,704
Here's how the location plays.

3
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:10,576
Put a Malice token in the Killer's start space and in three spaces next to it.

4
00:00:10,576 --> 00:00:14,773
If there are only two adjacent spaces, put the third in the next closest space of

5
00:00:14,773 --> 00:00:16,795
your choice. That's four Malice tokens.

6
00:00:17,015 --> 00:00:19,916
Put the Donkey token in the Cloister; cards refer to it.

7
00:00:20,136 --> 00:00:22,397
Add the Benediction Action cards to the Tableau.

8
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:27,430
The Blessed and Cursed dice sometimes replace a normal die in your Horror Rolls.

9
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:30,892
When you see one of their icons, swap one normal die for that one.

10
00:00:31,112 --> 00:00:33,977
The Blessed die is kinder: it shows two stars on a six.

11
00:00:33,977 --> 00:00:37,832
The Cursed die has fewer good faces, and a broken-heart symbol on its one.

12
00:00:38,052 --> 00:00:41,992
You never roll both. If there are more of one icon than the other, use that die.

13
00:00:41,992 --> 00:00:44,751
If they're equal, they cancel out and you roll normally.

14
00:00:44,971 --> 00:00:48,516
If your final Horror Roll shows the broken heart, you lose a health.

15
00:00:48,516 --> 00:00:52,373
And the Improvise card's effects also apply to the five on the Cursed die.

16
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:57,086
When you see the Malice icon, put a Malice token in the Active Killer's space.

17
00:00:57,086 --> 00:01:00,624
If it already has one, use the closest space to the Killer without one.

18
00:01:00,844 --> 00:01:03,887
With more than one Active Killer, use the one closest to you.

19
00:01:03,887 --> 00:01:07,927
With no Killer on the board, reveal a random Setup card and use its Killer space.

20
00:01:08,147 --> 00:01:12,370
Malice tokens carry the cursed symbol, so any Horror Roll you make in a Malice space

21
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:13,928
swaps a die for the Cursed die.

22
00:01:14,733 --> 00:01:18,617
There are fourteen Malice tokens. If all fourteen are on the board and you need to

23
00:01:18,617 --> 00:01:20,323
place another, you lose immediately.

24
00:01:20,543 --> 00:01:23,444
Tokens you remove go back into the pool, so keep clearing them.

25
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:27,253
Benediction is how you clear Malice. It costs one Time.

26
00:01:27,473 --> 00:01:31,881
The best result removes a Malice token from your space and every adjacent space.

27
00:01:31,881 --> 00:01:35,186
The next removes one from your space and one adjacent space.

28
00:01:35,186 --> 00:01:38,823
A weaker result removes one from your space or one adjacent space.

29
00:01:39,043 --> 00:01:41,368
The card's bottom row shows the cost of failing.

30
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:45,912
Black Mass adds a Malice token every Upkeep in which none was added.

31
00:01:45,912 --> 00:01:47,277
Treat it as an emergency.

32
00:01:47,497 --> 00:01:51,202
Father Damian follows you even into the Killer's space and gives you the Blessed die

33
00:01:51,202 --> 00:01:52,084
while he's with you.

34
00:01:52,304 --> 00:01:56,148
Lust kills the Victim closest to you in a Malice space, and hurts you if you're in

35
00:01:56,148 --> 00:01:56,336
one.

36
00:01:57,167 --> 00:02:01,561
A few tips. Use Benediction often: fourteen Malice tokens is an instant loss.

37
00:02:01,781 --> 00:02:05,195
Keep Victims out of the cursed rooms, and keep Father Damian close.

38
00:02:05,415 --> 00:02:08,065
The search spaces are far apart, so plan your route.

39
00:02:08,065 --> 00:02:10,409
It's rated one of the best boards in the game.

40
00:02:10,409 --> 00:02:10,919
Good luck.

